window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>They say the gods don’t give you more than you can handle, which is probably why I’m sinking in drama.</b></p> <p>As a god myself, I guess I’m not included in that little speech. But it’s about time they address me as who I am.</p> <p>Rhea.</p> <p>With my intentions questioned, and my battle far from over, the list of my enemies continues to grow. The Hex, Zellus, and what seems like the entire supernatural world. But I don’t stand alone, despite their efforts.</p> <p>Xander, Adonis, Zen, and Khaos.</p> <p>We are an unbreakable unit, forged in fire and sealed all the way down to our souls. I am theirs and they are mine.</p> <p>My shifter. My demon. My angel. My vampire.</p> <p>I may no longer be an earthling, but it’s clear I have traded one prison for another with Saints Academy. What they have yet to realize is I cannot be caged, and I will never stop fighting—for myself, my unit, or our freedom, worthy or not.</p> <p><i>Vicious Souls </i>is book three in the Saints Academy series.</p>"; 
